         "id": "SECTION_universe",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Everything Was Together\n\nModern measurements allow us to reconstruct the history of the universe, from its very beginning to the present day. Use the arrows to travel step by step through this history, from the universe today back to the Big Bang.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"3000\" data-x1=\"5000\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>13.82 Billion Years — The Universe Today</h4><p>This is the universe as we see it today: clusters of galaxies, our own galaxy the Milky Way, and our solar system around an ordinary star.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 7</div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"2050\" data-x1=\"3000\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>1 to 13.82 Billion Years — Galaxy Evolution</h4><p>Galaxies grow and merge into larger systems. Along the filaments of dark matter, clusters of galaxies and superclusters form the cosmic web.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 7</div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"1700\" data-x1=\"2050\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>200 Million to 1 Billion Years — The First Stars and Galaxies</h4><p>The first stars ignite, ending the dark ages. Their light ionizes the surrounding gas, and the first galaxies begin to take shape.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">3 / 7</div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"1150\" data-x1=\"1700\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>380,000 Years to 200 Million Years — Recombination, the CMB and the Dark Ages</h4><p>The universe cools enough for electrons and nuclei to join into atoms: matter decouples from light and the Cosmic Microwave Background is released — the oldest light we can still observe. With no free electrons the universe becomes transparent and dark, and matter falls into the structures formed by dark matter, slowly building the scaffolding of the galaxies to come.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">4 / 7</div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"750\" data-x1=\"1150\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>100 Seconds to 380,000 Years — Matter and Light Are Coupled</h4><p>Ordinary matter particles are coupled to light, forming a hot, opaque plasma. Dark matter particles begin to build structures, gently pulling matter together through gravity.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">5 / 7</div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"650\" data-x1=\"750\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>1 to 100 Seconds — Particles Form</h4><p>As the universe cools, energy turns into the first particles: protons, neutrons and electrons, together with their antiparticles. Matter and antimatter mostly annihilate, leaving a small surplus of matter that will build everything we see.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">6 / 7</div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htUniverseFrame\"><div class=\"htUniverseClip\"><img class=\"htUniverseImg\" data-x0=\"350\" data-x1=\"650\" alt=\"\"/></div></div><h4>0 to 1 Second — Big Bang and Cosmic Inflation</h4><p>Everything that exists begins in an extremely hot and dense point. In a fraction of a second, cosmic inflation stretches space faster than light, smoothing it out and creating the tiny seeds of all the structures to come.</p><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">7 / 7</div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\" aria-label=\"Previous slide\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\" aria-label=\"Next slide\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></div></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 1</b>: Planck history of the Universe. ESA — C. Carreau (<htcite0>).</p>",
