      {
         "id": "SECTION_reflection",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Reflection\n\nThe image we observed in this class shows us that the information we obtain from the universe indicates that everything was concentrated at the beginning.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection: Everything Was Together</b><br /><br />Do these measurements agree with the understanding of Lavoisier that we studied in previous classes?</div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgPlanckFull\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgPlanckFull', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: Planck history of Universe. ©ESA – C. Carreau (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a1a7c478-9061-4160-ba43-301c081733e9",
                     "text": "ESA",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "09",
                        "day": "17"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "The answer to this reflection is found in the conclusion of this text.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nIn the beginning, everything in the universe was one. Matter and energy were united in a single, extremely hot and dense point. The measurements we observe today, together with what Lavoisier taught us — nothing is lost, nothing is created, everything is transformed — show us that we and all things around us share the same origin.\n\nTherefore, everything and everybody has the same origin: the matter and the energy that today form galaxies, stars, planets, and life itself were all together at the beginning. Starting in the next text of the *First Steps* section (<htcite0>), we will study this process of sharing matter and energy.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "58da6d75-ce8a-45f5-b57f-1f0763ee3568",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Simplicity vs. Complexity",
                     "date_time": {
